C. Proof-shaped consequence
  Since Q27 infeasibility implies Q31 infeasibility, the 489 first-pass
  infeasible cases need no widening.  The four timeout cases are Q27
  infeasible after a longer limit.  The only two Q27-feasible deletion
  shapes are Q31-infeasible.  Therefore, inside the carry window, every
  primitive replacement row retaining at least 8 core speeds has a Q31
  witness.  The bounded descent portal starts at <=7 retained core speeds,
  unless the row leaves the window or opens an owner/Bprime exception.
